%I A401037 #6 Oct 26 2026 21:52:55
%S A401037 0,2,0,3,2,5,2,18,8,4,2,15,0,4,0,13
%N A401037 Number of orbits of exponents d, 1 <= d <= 2^n-2, under multiplication by 2 modulo 2^n-1, such that the power map x -> x^d on GF(2^n) has differential uniformity 4.
%C A401037 The differential uniformity of x^d on GF(2^n) is the maximum, over a != 0 and b in GF(2^n), of the number of solutions x of (x+a)^d + x^d = b. For a power map it suffices to take a = 1. Differential uniformity 2 corresponds to almost perfect nonlinear power maps; the corresponding count is A400802.
%e A401037 a(4) = 2: modulo 15, the orbits {5, 10} and {7, 11, 13, 14} are the only ones for which x^d has differential uniformity 4.
%o A401037 (PARI) a(n) = {my(M=2^n-1, g=ffprimroot(ffgen(2^n, 'z)), X=concat([0*g], vector(M, i, g^i)), c=0, e, ok, v, mx, r, f); for(d=1, M-1, e=d; ok=1; for(i=1, n-1, e=2*e%M; if(e<d, ok=0; break)); if(!ok, next); v=vecsort(vector(2^n, i, f=(X[i]+1)^d+X[i]^d; if(f==0, -1, fflog(f, g)))); mx=1; r=1; for(i=2, #v, if(v[i]==v[i-1], r++; mx=max(mx, r), r=1)); if(mx==4, c++)); c}
%Y A401037 Cf. A400802.
%K A401037 nonn,more,new
%O A401037 3,2
%A A401037 _Sajid Khan Hussain_, Oct 14 2026
